<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · concept</p><h1 class="enc-title">Central bank</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as central banking</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">A central bank is a public institution that manages a state's currency, money supply and banking system. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a>'s Riksbank, founded in 1668, is generally considered the oldest central bank still in operation. Its creation by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swedish-empire">Swedish Empire</a> contributed to the development of modern central banking concepts.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/central-bank.jpg" alt="Central bank" width="320" height="248" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dan Smith · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Federal_Reserve.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
